<title>UK: Zambia Copper Mines says two killed in rockfall.</title>
<headline>Zambia Copper Mines says two killed in rockfall.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zambia Consolidated Copper Mines Ltd said on Thursday that two contractors had been killed in a rockfall accident at the 990 metre level of its Muflulira Division underground mine.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement released in London that a seismic event which rocked the mine without warning on July 1 left five other contractors injured. They were rescued the following day.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been no interruption of other mining operators which continue as normal,&quot; the group added.</p>
<p>The mining giant, whose shares are floated on the Paris stock exchange, accounts for about 90 percent of Zambia's export earnings.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7987</p>
